---
description: 
globs: 
alwaysApply: false
---


# 1. Dependency Directories
# These contain thousands of files from third-party libraries and are not part of our source code.
# Including them would consume the entire context window with irrelevant information.
node_modules/

# 2. Build & Compilation Output
# These directories contain the compiled, minified, or bundled output of our applications.
# The AI should work with the source code, not the generated artifacts.
/dist
/build
.svelte-kit/
.vite/


# 4. Infrastructure as Code (IaC) State & Logs
# Terraform state files can contain sensitive infrastructure details. The .terraform
# directory contains provider plugins and is not needed for context.
.terraform/
terraform.tfstate
terraform.tfstate.backup
*.tfvars

# 5. Logs & Reports
# Log files and test reports are runtime artifacts and not relevant for code generation.
logs/
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log
coverage/
.nyc_output/

# 6. Version Control & OS/IDE Files
# These are metadata files for Git, operating systems, and specific IDEs. They are
# not relevant to the project's source code.
.git/
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/

# 7. Package Manager Lock Files
# While crucial for dependency management, these files are very large and don't
# provide useful context for generating new features or refactoring code.
package-lock.json
yarn.lock
pnpm-lock.yaml

# 8. Kubernetes Manifests (Optional - uncomment if needed)
# By default, we ignore the Kubernetes directory. For deployment-related tasks,
# you should explicitly add this directory or specific files to your prompt
# using the `@kubernetes/` command in the chat.

# kubernetes/